{{!-- Kleinkram: Papiere und Krimskrams — carried gear the inventory rules price
at zero slots, so it never occupies a cell in the Trageslots raster and gets a
tab of its own beside the wallet instead. The tab button carries the
explanation; money balances live in the other tab.

The list has no create control and no drop target of its own. Nothing here is
a state a piece can be put *into*: an item is Kleinkram exactly when its
`slots` is 0, which is authored on the item's own sheet. Same interactions as a
slot cell otherwise — costing nothing to carry does not make it a different kind
of thing, so it can still be opened, sorted and worn.

The filter is client-side like the skill search, so typing costs no re-render. --}}
<div class='slot-trinkets'>

  {{#if slotGrid.trinkets.length}}
    <input type='text' class='trinket-filter-input' value='{{trinketFilter}}'
           placeholder='{{localize "TNO.Inventory.TrinketsFilter"}}'
           title='{{localize "TNO.Inventory.TrinketsFilterHint"}}' aria-label='{{localize "TNO.Inventory.TrinketsFilterHint"}}' />
    <div class='slot-trinkets-list'>
      {{#each slotGrid.trinkets as |trinket|}}
        <span class='slot-trinket draggable' data-item-id='{{trinket.item._id}}'>
          {{#if trinket.img}}
            <img class='slot-trinket-icon slot-art' src='{{trinket.img}}' alt='' />
          {{else}}
            <i class='fa-solid {{trinket.icon}} slot-trinket-icon' aria-hidden='true'></i>
          {{/if}}
          <span class='slot-trinket-name' title='{{trinket.item.name}}'>{{trinket.item.name}}</span>
          <span class='slot-trinket-qty'>{{trinket.quantity}}</span>
        </span>
      {{/each}}
      <p class='slot-trinkets-empty slot-trinkets-nomatch' hidden>{{localize 'TNO.Inventory.TrinketsNoMatch'}}</p>
    </div>
  {{else}}
    <p class='slot-trinkets-empty'>{{localize 'TNO.Inventory.TrinketsEmpty'}}</p>
  {{/if}}

</div>
